core-terminal (0.2.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Restore the Text profile form and load its controls from the active
    profile.
  * Make Text-page scrollback the canonical per-profile value, preserve
    unlimited and low values, and keep the Window-page field read-only.
  * Migrate legacy global input-scroll, bell, and bright-bold flags into all
    profiles once during upgrade.
  * Store Homebrew's font family and size as separate values.
  * Preserve imported values for unavailable and renderer-owned settings.
  * Keep startup, tab, window, and Window Group launch policies independent.
  * Revalidate close requests and clean complete native and Flatpak sessions.
  * Exercise job control, terminal resizing, signals, and exit status over a
    PTY.
  * Add a standard menubar and terminal context menu, and keep titlebar
    controls compositor-owned.
  * Make the profile editor responsive instead of enforcing a desktop-sized
    minimum allocation.
  * Disable ThinLTO in the release profile to avoid the observed Ubuntu
    Rust/LLVM compiler crash.

 -- Kasey <211167966+ksudo-dev@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 04 Sep 2026 01:17:22 -0700

core-terminal (0.2.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Make the bottom Settings Save action authoritative for Window Groups.
  * Add, remove, edit, and reorder every tab in a saved Window Group.
  * Protect profiles referenced by groups and validate saved directories.
  * Preserve the host login shell and desktop session environment in Flatpak.
  * Remove Flatpak development files and expand release checks.

 -- Kasey <211167966+ksudo-dev@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 03 Sep 2026 17:45:00 -0700

core-terminal (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add the GTK4/VTE settings panes and profile editor paths.
  * Wire keyboard input, shell exit, title, notification, and saved group
    settings to the terminal runtime.
  * Add the native Wayland acceptance harness.
  * Keep profile names, labeled actions, and editor tabs visible without an
    outer horizontal settings scroller.
  * Add Debian metadata, the core-terminal(1) manual page, and dependency
    license notices.
  * Reject private profile and reference inputs during package checks.

